\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Leave-one-paper-out. Confidence is disagreement-aware. The evidence column reports $n$, the total grounded exemplars (which sets $E=\min (1,n/6)$), and in parentheses the cleavable/non-cleavable split among the cleavage-labelled ones (which sets the consensus $\kappa $); e.g.\ ISAC $5\,(1/0)$ gives $E=5/6$, $\kappa =1$, $C=0.83$. The ARC rule flips direction and loses confidence because its evidence is genuinely divided ($4/2$).\relax }}{3}{table.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:heldout}{{1}{3}{Leave-one-paper-out. Confidence is disagreement-aware. The evidence column reports $n$, the total grounded exemplars (which sets $E=\min (1,n/6)$), and in parentheses the cleavable/non-cleavable split among the cleavage-labelled ones (which sets the consensus $\kappa $); e.g.\ ISAC $5\,(1/0)$ gives $E=5/6$, $\kappa =1$, $C=0.83$. The ARC rule flips direction and loses confidence because its evidence is genuinely divided ($4/2$).\relax }{table.caption.2}{}}
