\newlabel{tab:short}{{2}{3}{One representative generated design per class (all fifteen with full dossiers in the SI). SA = continuous Ertl synthetic-accessibility subscore; Stab = mechanism-resolved plasma-stability score.\relax }{table.caption.6}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {4}Discussion}{3}{section.4}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Held-out test. Left: full-corpus vs held-out confidence (disagreement-aware); the ARC rule flips (amber) while cytotoxin/ISAC recover (indigo), the dotted line marking the 0.5 contested floor. Right: the grounded-evidence split that explains it---ARC is 4:2 (contested), the others unanimous (cleavable purple, non-cleavable orange).\relax }}{4}{figure.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:heldout}{{2}{4}{Held-out test. Left: full-corpus vs held-out confidence (disagreement-aware); the ARC rule flips (amber) while cytotoxin/ISAC recover (indigo), the dotted line marking the 0.5 contested floor. Right: the grounded-evidence split that explains it---ARC is 4:2 (contested), the others unanimous (cleavable purple, non-cleavable orange).\relax }{figure.caption.3}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The rules steer the chemistry, in three panels. \textbf  {(a)} the compiled objective weights---a deterministic rule-compilation (a heuristic keyed by the agent's derived category, effectively three buckets, not continuously tuned); the ``rigidity'' term rewards \emph  {fewer} rotatable bonds, so the real separator is the per-class rotatable-bond setpoint (rot$\leq $5/10/14) shown by each class, and ISAC's stability weight is floored to paramount by the low-evidence safety gate. \textbf  {(b)} the generated designs in rotatable-bond\,$\times $\,Ertl-SA space---colour encodes the target (cyto/ISAC/ARC), marker shape whether the linker is cleavable ($\circ $) or non-cleavable ($\times $); they separate mainly along the rigidity setpoint. \textbf  {(c)} the actual generated molecules with their scores, drawn with SMARTS-detected handle (blue), scissile bond (red) and spacer (green)---each a real REINVENT design carrying its literature-derived motif. The ARC molecules carry a rigid non-cleavable DBCO cap (no scissile bond), which stands in for the same rigid non-cleavable class as the clinical sulfo-SMCC/MCC benchmark.\relax }}{4}{figure.caption.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:steer}{{3}{4}{The rules steer the chemistry, in three panels. \textbf {(a)} the compiled objective weights---a deterministic rule-compilation (a heuristic keyed by the agent's derived category, effectively three buckets, not continuously tuned); the ``rigidity'' term rewards \emph {fewer} rotatable bonds, so the real separator is the per-class rotatable-bond setpoint (rot$\leq $5/10/14) shown by each class, and ISAC's stability weight is floored to paramount by the low-evidence safety gate. \textbf {(b)} the generated designs in rotatable-bond\,$\times $\,Ertl-SA space---colour encodes the target (cyto/ISAC/ARC), marker shape whether the linker is cleavable ($\circ $) or non-cleavable ($\times $); they separate mainly along the rigidity setpoint. \textbf {(c)} the actual generated molecules with their scores, drawn with SMARTS-detected handle (blue), scissile bond (red) and spacer (green)---each a real REINVENT design carrying its literature-derived motif. The ARC molecules carry a rigid non-cleavable DBCO cap (no scissile bond), which stands in for the same rigid non-cleavable class as the clinical sulfo-SMCC/MCC benchmark.\relax }{figure.caption.4}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Stress-test of the confidence metric: varying retrieval depth (top-$k$) leaves each class's confidence stable---the ARC rule stays contested ($\approx $0.33) at every $k$. Reproducible, not a lucky $k$.\relax }}{4}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:sens}{{4}{4}{Stress-test of the confidence metric: varying retrieval depth (top-$k$) leaves each class's confidence stable---the ARC rule stays contested ($\approx $0.33) at every $k$. Reproducible, not a lucky $k$.\relax }{figure.caption.5}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Cathepsin-B co-fold (affinity indexes recognition, not cleavage). The cleavable Val-Cit designs (cytotoxin, and the held-out-derived ARC linker) are recognised in the clinical-substrate regime; the rigid ARC design binds $>$10$\times $ weaker---the in-silico feasibility proof.\relax }}{4}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cofold}{{5}{4}{Cathepsin-B co-fold (affinity indexes recognition, not cleavage). The cleavable Val-Cit designs (cytotoxin, and the held-out-derived ARC linker) are recognised in the clinical-substrate regime; the rigid ARC design binds $>$10$\times $ weaker---the in-silico feasibility proof.\relax }{figure.caption.5}{}}
